<%# 
====================================================================
FILE: src/views/login.ejs
COURSE: CSE 340 - Web Backend Development (Week 5)
====================================================================
PLAIN ENGLISH: The sign-in page where a registered person logs in.
LOGIC: Shown by showLoginForm (GET /login). When submitted, the form sends
       email and password to POST /login (processLoginForm).
WHY WE NEED IT: People need a form to prove who they are (authentication).
LEARNING GAP: Only email and password are needed here, not name. The server
              looks up the user by email in the users table, then bcrypt
              compares the typed password to the stored hash.
%>
<%- include('partials/header') %>
    <main>
        <%# title comes from the controller: res.render('login', { title: 'Login' }) %>
        <h1><%= title %></h1>

        <%# 
        PLAIN ENGLISH: The login form.
        LOGIC: method="POST" sends the data in the request body.
               action="/login" sends it to the POST /login route.
        WHY WE NEED IT: Connects this form to processLoginForm.
        LEARNING GAP: POST keeps the password out of the web address bar and
                      browser history, which GET would expose.
        %>
        <form action="/login" method="POST">

            <%# 
            PLAIN ENGLISH: Email box (the username).
            LOGIC: name="email" becomes req.body.email in the controller.
            WHY WE NEED IT: The server finds the account by email (findUserByEmail).
            LEARNING GAP: Must be the same email used when registering.
            %>
            <div class="form-group">
                <label for="email">Email (Username)</label>
                <input
                    type="email"
                    id="email"
                    name="email"
                    required
                />
            </div>

            <%# 
            PLAIN ENGLISH: Password box.
            LOGIC: name="password" becomes req.body.password in the controller.
            WHY WE NEED IT: bcrypt.compare checks it against the stored hash.
            LEARNING GAP: The typed password is never saved. It's only compared,
                          then thrown away.
            %>
            <div class="form-group">
                <label for="password">Password</label>
                <input
                    type="password"
                    id="password"
                    name="password"
                    required
                />
            </div>
            <button type="submit">Login</button>
        </form>
    </main>   

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
